    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive outlook centers on **Mickey Moniak**, who stands as our premier play at 75.98. His start against the right-handed Roki Sasaki is an ideal configuration; the combination of a favorable park factor (+14%) and the advantage of Sasaki\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which elevates our steal probability to 88%\u2014makes him a cornerstone for speed and production. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (64.59) and **Isaac Paredes** (64.31) offer high-floor utility. **Jose Caballero** benefits from a massive park boost and a matchup against a soft-tossing Chris Bassitt, while **Isaac Paredes** enjoys significant platoon leverage against Walbert Ure\u00f1a, allowing him to capitalize on the +9% dynamic platoon modifier despite a middling base projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer involved **Vinnie Pasquantino** (55.65), who just narrowly missed the cut. While his raw projection was competitive, the volatility of the mid-order lineup spots and the higher ceiling provided by **Austin Riley**\u2014who benefits from a favorable \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus against Taj Bradley\u2014pushed **Vinnie Pasquantino** to the bench. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Corbin Carroll** (56.41). While his speed is elite, the presence of Payton Tolle on the mound creates a significant \"Elite Hold\" risk for our stolen base targets; his overall score is suppressed by that matchup, though he remains a vital fixture in the outfield. \n\nWe are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions for the entire roster, meaning any late-breaking changes to batting order placements\u2014particularly for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang**\u2014could necessitate a shift in our daily efficiency outlook. While **Brice Turang** holds a strong 53.55 score due to his likely leadoff spot, the matchup against Logan Gilbert\u2019s elite skill set remains a pivot point for his production. Our primary objective remains insulating the roster from sub-40 floor performances, which is why **Zach McKinstry** remains benched; he is unable to overcome the negative modifiers associated with Paul Skenes\u2019 elite arm and defensive efficiency.",
